; controls-vector: xy + color control types under the corpus gate. pan
; is an xy widget (ncomp 2) with [-1,1] rails on both lanes; tint is a
; color widget (ncomp 3), which carries NO rails — `(control …)` is
; discriminated on :type and the range keys live in the variant slider
; and xy select, so `:min` on a colour picker is unknown_key. Both target
; a host registry slot, so each document :value writes every idle frame
; and a live drv_setControl vector override wins until cleared — pinning
; vector control set/clear across the wasm boundary and the :type /
; :min / :max echo through 'PACM' for the non-scalar control kinds.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4])

(control :id pan  :type xy    :target pan-out  :min [-1 -1] :max [1 1] :value [0.25 0.5])
(control :id tint :type color :target tint-out :value [0.2 0.4 0.6])
